  "claim": "The song, which Billie Anthony is best known for her Top 10 hit version, topped the UK chart in 1981 in a recording by a platinum-selling Welsh rock and roll singer whose recording and performing career began in the late 1960s.",
  "evidencia": "Page: This Ole House. Sentence: \"This Ole House\" (sometimes written \"This Old House\") is a popular song written by Stuart Hamblen, and published in 1954.\nPage: This Ole House. Sentence: The song again topped the UK chart in 1981 in a recording by Shakin' Stevens.\nPage: Shakin' Stevens. Sentence: Michael Barratt (born 4 March 1948), known as Shakin' Stevens, is a platinum-selling British rock and roll singer and songwriter who was the UK's biggest-selling singles artist of the 1980s.\nPage: Shakin' Stevens. Sentence: His recording and performing career began in the late 1960s, although it was not until 1980 that his commercial success began.\nPage: Billie Anthony. Sentence: She is best known for her Top 10 hit version of \"This Ole House\", which despite chart competition from other versions of the same song, reached No. 4 in the UK chart.",
