        "original_id": "4d17f4d2-6a82-582a-97af-833933a79c15",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stuart Hamblen, Shakin' Stevens, Michael Barratt, Billie Anthony\n- Works: \"This Ole House\"\n- Topics: UK music charts, recording careers\n\nFacts:\n- Stuart Hamblen wrote the popular song \"This Ole House,\" sometimes written \"This Old House,\" and the song was published in 1954.\n- Shakin' Stevens is the stage name of Michael Barratt, who was born on 4 March 1948.\n- Shakin' Stevens began his recording and performing career in the late 1960s.\n- Shakin' Stevens' commercial success began in 1980.\n- Shakin' Stevens was the UK's biggest-selling singles artist of the 1980s and was a platinum-selling British rock and roll singer and songwriter.\n- In 1981, Shakin' Stevens' recording of \"This Ole House\" topped the UK chart.\n- Billie Anthony is best known for her Top 10 version of \"This Ole House,\" which reached No. 4 on the UK chart despite competition from other versions of the song.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "96efd7d1-26db-522e-97b0-35d6cf2f9577",
        "text": "Page: This Ole House. Sentence: \"This Ole House\" (sometimes written \"This Old House\") is a popular song written by Stuart Hamblen, and published in 1954.\nPage: This Ole House. Sentence: The song again topped the UK chart in 1981 in a recording by Shakin' Stevens.\nPage: Shakin' Stevens. Sentence: Michael Barratt (born 4 March 1948), known as Shakin' Stevens, is a platinum-selling British rock and roll singer and songwriter who was the UK's biggest-selling singles artist of the 1980s.\nPage: Shakin' Stevens. Sentence: His recording and performing career began in the late 1960s, although it was not until 1980 that his commercial success began.\nPage: Billie Anthony. Sentence: She is best known for her Top 10 hit version of \"This Ole House\", which despite chart competition from other versions of the same song, reached No. 4 in the UK chart.",
